\f0\b\fs26 \cf0 Trimmomatic
\b0\fs20 \
versatile tool to trim and filter reads\
filter:			exclude certain reads based on certain specifics\
trim:			remove parts of reads to reach better quality\
\
install with conda and you can run it directly with command:\
$ trimmomatic .......\
\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\b \cf0 general syntax:
\b0 \
$ trimmomatic SE [-phred33|64] -trimlog <logFile> <inputfile> outputfile <filter1> <filter2> .....\
or for paired reads:\
$ trimmomatic PE [-phred33|64]  -trimlog <logFile>  -basein <inputfile1> -baseout <outputfile1>\
using -basein and -baseout lets trimmomatic autodetect the pairs using different naming schemes\
if you use -baseout option the following naming convention is used:\
<outputfile1>_1P.fq.gz 	for paired forward reads\
<outputfile1>_1U.fq.gz 	for unpaired forward reads\
<outputfile1>_2P.fq.gz 	for paired reverse reads\
<outputfile1>_2U.fq.gz 	for unpaired reverse reads\
\
